  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Worlds should be able to provide an exposure compensation recommendation to the camera. \nNothing extreme, mostly thinking about dim hangout worlds. Right now you can tune your world for a nice feel in VR, and have dark photos by default. \n\nIt would be cool to tell the camera to go a stop or two brighter by default. \n\nEnforcing a rage limit would be nice to prevent abuse. But like everyone always says, if a world mucks with the camera in a negative way, vote with your attention. So maybe that is a non-issue.\n\nThanks.\n\nEdit: I conflated VRC Lens with the new camera when it comes to exposure controls. I guess those are needed too. That is a separate feature request already in the feedback boards.",
